   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = x y + 1 \\) with \\( f(0) = 1 \\). Find the approximation to \\( f(-1) \\) given by Euler's method, starting at \\( x = 0 \\) with two steps of equal size. Give the exact value."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         8
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The step size is \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{-1 - (0)}{2} = - \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (0, 1) \\) the slope is \\( 1 \\), so \\( y \\approx 1 + (- \\frac{1}{2})(1) = \\frac{1}{2} \\) at \\( x = - \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (- \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}) \\) the slope is \\( \\frac{3}{4} \\), so \\( y \\approx \\frac{1}{2} + (- \\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{3}{4}) = \\frac{1}{8} \\) at \\( x = -1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( f(-1) \\approx \\frac{1}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            8
         ]
      }
   ],
